*.log
# RotatingFileHandler's numbered backups; `*.log` does not match them
*.log.[0-9]*
# Atomic-write staging files (utils.write_json_atomic). The `*.json` rule below does NOT
# match a `.tmp` suffix, so without these a crash between the write and the os.replace
# leaves a multi-megabyte state dump sitting committable in the working tree. Both forms
# are listed: the plain one for older leftovers, the PID form the writer uses now.
*.json.tmp
*.json.*.tmp
# The reaper claims the deletions queue by renaming it aside; same reasoning.
*.jsonl.processing
__pycache__/
.DS_Store
*.json
*.jsonl
.host_mode
.claude
.codex
.vscode
# Runtime lock: created per-process, must never be version-controlled
upload.lock
# 24 MB of random bytes benchmark_exit_nodes.py uploads to measure a node. It removes this on
# exit, including on Ctrl-C; the entry exists so a crash in between cannot leave it committable.
.exit_probe_payload.bin

# One-off state backups taken before a migration (see README "Renaming or
# Restructuring a Title"). Local rollback copies, never history.
*.bak-*
